      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T00:06:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The two cases are in the message now. Could the first paragraph also say what goes wrong in each? \"pins and accounts native pages\" doesn\u0027t say why that breaks for a 4KB process. Something like:\n\n```\nVFIO type1 pins and maps whole kernel pages, but the 4KB pages of a\n16KB range in a 4KB process can be slices of different kernel pages,\nso the IOMMU could map memory outside the range. Device mmap()\nhandlers such as vfio_platform_mmap_mmio() also ignore vm_slice_off,\nso an offset that isn\u0027t 16KB-aligned maps MMIO past the region.\n```",
      "parentUuid": "0029ce17_f46a970a",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "4988ff901d7c9635d69338a4c41cf65473605672",
